.include "shift.jsim"

.checkoff "" "ALU: shift module"  0

* 1. Instantiate your shift module
* Input: sfn[1:0] -- 2-bit for selecting shifting function.
*        A[31:0] -- 32-bit input to be shifted
*        B[4:0] -- 5-bit input specifying number of shifting bits (0 to 31)
* Output: sh[31:0] -- result of the shifting

Xshift sfn[1:0] A[31:0] B[4:0] sh[31:0] shift

* 2. Generate input vector
* Inputs: sfn[1:0], A[31:0], B[4:0]
* Generate following test vectors
* The inputs change every 100ns

Wfn sfn[1:0] nrz(0,3.3,100n,0n,.1n,.1n) 
+ 0b00 0b01 0b11
